.(KLONDIKE - DRAFT. Uses proposed syntax, so it doesn't parse yet.
  Proposals used: 1 let, 2 none, 3 face up and face down, 4 numbered piles,
  5 :top and :pile, 6 from, 7 in, 9 first, 16 must, 17 card:colour.
  See PROPOSALS.md.

  HOW TO PLAY

  Klondike is the classic patience game for one player. The aim is to move
  every card onto four foundations, one per suit, from Ace up to King.

  The layout
    Shuffle, then deal seven columns. Column 1 gets 1 card, column 2 gets 2,
    and so on up to column 7 with 7 cards. Every card is face down except
    the top card of each column. The rest of the deck is the stock.

  Your turn
    Do one of these:
    - draw: turn the top card of the stock face up onto the waste pile.
      When the stock is empty, turn the waste over to make a new stock.
    - put: move a face-up card onto a column whose top card is one higher
      and the other colour. For example, a red 7 goes on a black 8. Any
      cards on top of it in its column move with it. Write the card to move
      and the card to put it on: put 7h / 8s
    - space: move a King, and any cards on top of it, into an empty column:
      space kh
    - home: move a card to its foundation. An Ace starts a foundation; after
      that each card must be the next one up in the same suit: home 2h
    Cards can be moved from the waste or a foundation, but only the top card.
    When a column's top card is face down, it is turned face up.

  Winning
    You win when all 52 cards are on the foundations. Type resign to give up.)

name klondike
players 1

stack stock face down
stack waste
stack foundations 4
stack columns 7


def setup(){
    shuffle(deck)
    every pile column in columns {
        deck > column column:id face down    .(column 1 gets 1 card, column 7 gets 7)
        turn_up(column:top)
    }
    deck > stock end
}


.(Moves)

move draw(player){
    if(count(stock) is 0){
        must(count(waste) > 0, there are no cards left to draw)
        waste > stock end    .(turning the waste over makes it the stock again)
    } else {
        stock > waste
    }
}

move put(player, moving, onto){
    must(count(moving) is 1 & count(onto) is 1, name the card to move and the card to put it on, e.g. put 7h / 8s)
    let card = moving:top
    let target = onto:top
    must(can_lift(card), you can only move a face-up card, and only the top card of the waste or a foundation)
    must(target:pile in columns & target is target:pile:top, you can only put cards on the top card of a column)
    must(card:value is target:value - 1, it must be one lower than the card it goes on)
    must(card:colour is not target:colour, it must be the other colour)
    card:pile > target:pile from card
}

move space(player, moving){
    must(count(moving) is 1, name the king to move, e.g. space kh)
    let card = moving:top
    must(card:rank is King, only a king can go in an empty column)
    must(can_lift(card), you can only move a face-up card, and only the top card of the waste or a foundation)
    let space = first pile column in columns: count(column) is 0
    must(space is not none, there's no empty column)
    card:pile > space from card
}

move home(player, moving){
    must(count(moving) is 1, name the card to move, e.g. home 2h)
    let card = moving:top
    must(card:face_up & card is card:pile:top, only the top card of a pile can go home)
    let foundation = first pile f in foundations: goes_home(card, f)
    must(foundation is not none, that card can't go home yet: it needs the card one below it in the same suit)
    card:pile > foundation from card
}

move resign(player){
    end()
}


.(after_move runs after every successful move)
def after_move(){
    every pile column in columns {
        turn_up(column:top)    .(does nothing if it's already face up, or the column is empty)
    }
    if(every pile f in foundations: count(f) is 13){
        winner(1)
        end()
    }
}


.(Rules about cards)

.(from a column you can lift any face-up card, with the cards on top of it;
  from the waste or a foundation, only the top card)
def can_lift(card){
    return(card:face_up & (card:pile in columns or card is card:pile:top))
}

.(an Ace goes on an empty foundation; anything else on the card one below it in the same suit)
def goes_home(card, foundation){
    if(count(foundation) is 0){
        return(card:rank is Ace)
    }
    return(card:suit is foundation:top:suit & card:value is foundation:top:value + 1)
}
